  "result": "Reservations with expiry are in, and `npm test` passes (177 tests, 0 failed).\n\n**Store (`src/store.js`)**\n- `reserve`, `getAvailable`, `confirm` and `release` are added as specified.\n- `removeItem` now throws `INSUFFICIENT_STOCK` when `qty` is more than what is available, so reserved stock can't be removed.\n- Time comes only from the store's `clock`.\n- Reservation ids are `res-1`, `res-2` and so on.\n- `confirm` returns `{sku, stock}`; the spec didn't ask for a return value, so say if you'd rather it return nothing.\n- A reservation expired at its `clock() >= creation + ttlMs` cutoff stays in the map and is never cleaned up. Confirming it keeps throwing `RESERVATION_EXPIRED`.\n\n**API (`src/api.js`)**\n- `GET /stock/:sku` also returns `available`.\n- `POST /reservations` returns 201 `{id}`, 409 `INSUFFICIENT_STOCK` or 400 `INVALID_QTY`.\n- `POST /reservations/:id/confirm` returns 200 `{sku, stock}`, 404 `RESERVATION_NOT_FOUND` or 410 `RESERVATION_EXPIRED`.\n- `DELETE /reservations/:id` returns 204, including for unknown or already-released ids.\n\n**Tests**\nI added 8 store tests and 4 API tests, driven by a controllable clock. They cover:\n- the exact expiry boundary\n- confirm and release, including repeats and unknown ids\n- `removeItem` blocked by reserved stock, and allowed again once the reservation expires\n- every API status code\n\nThe existing 165 tests still pass.\n\nI added no validation of `ttlMs`, since the spec doesn't ask for any.",
